      "lineNbr": 47,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003195
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-02T16:30:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What happens if the device NACKs part of the block read or returns fewer bytes than mfrModelReadLen? Please validate rbuf.size() before calling subspan(1, 4)",
      "revId": "3b474c42e4f121a93f0e0b94053e45d92d935f09",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6c9f793f_8a8275d3",
        "filename": "i2c-vr/mps/mpq82d00.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 47,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002589
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-03T06:46:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the suggestion.\n\nIf the device NACKs, I2C::sendReceive() returns false because ioctl(I2C_RDWR) fails, and checkId() returns false in that case.\n\nrbuf is resized to mfrIdReadLen / mfrModelReadLen before each read, and sendReceive() does not change its size, so the buffer size is currently guaranteed by the caller.\n\nI\u0027ve also added explicit rbuf.size() checks before both subspan(1) for MFR_ID and subspan(1, 4) for MFR_MODEL, so the bounds are now validated locally before creating the subspans.",
      "parentUuid": "ce421afd_1ee4f7d8",
      "revId": "3b474c42e4f121a93f0e0b94053e45d92d935f09",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "21834bda_4910e3b1",
        "filename": "i2c-vr/mps/mpq82d00.cpp",
